<!--
    PUF Invoice Example: France B2G simple invoice

    Use Case: A private supplier sends a simple mixed invoice to a French public buyer through Chorus Pro.
    This is the PUF source counterpart of AIFE qualification scenario 1.1.

    Country: France
    Format: PUF (Pagero Universal Format) 2.0
    Document Type: Invoice (Type 380)
    Transaction Type: M1 - mixed goods and services invoice
    Target Format: France UBL EXTENDED-CTC-FR V1.4

    Scenario Description:
    MADMAN invoices Mairie B for EUR 10,000.00 net plus EUR 1,000.00 VAT. The two lines
    reference separate public commitments and deliveries. SERV_EXE is the buyer reference;
    FACTURES_IMMO is the distinct public-buyer service code.

    CRITICAL - QUALIFICATION ADDRESSING:
    The 0225 endpoints are values from the AIFE qualification fixture. They are test values,
    not a general rule for constructing French electronic addresses.

    Key Fields:
    - BR-FR-CPRO-00: #ADN#B2G activates the Chorus Pro B2G rules.
    - BR-FR-CPRO-09/10: Seller and public buyer SIRETs use scheme 0009.
    - BT-10: BuyerReference is SERV_EXE and is separate from FR:ServiceCode.
    - EXT-FR-FE-135 and EXT-FR-FE-140/141: Line-level order and delivery references.

    Note: BAR is mandatory for non-B2G France scenarios but is not required for B2G and is
    deliberately omitted here.

    Reference: AIFE Chorus Pro qualification scenario 1.1; XP Z12-012 V1.4 BR-FR-CPRO-00,
    BR-FR-CPRO-09 and BR-FR-CPRO-10.
-->
